    "name": "Fresh Harvested Chestnuts",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">These are fresh, NOT dried chestnuts.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Cure them by spreading them out at room temperature for 3 to 4 days to convert starches into natural sugars, enhancing sweetness. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Cooking:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> Always cook and peel chestnuts before eating; never eat them raw straight off the tree due to high tannin content and tough texture. Score the outer shell and roast at 350°F for 25 minutes or steam them to make peeling easier.</span></p>",
